Sweep design:
  Source cells: 3 (CID22-512 1420710, 1531677, 1189261 — F-D residual cluster)
  Distances: {3, 4, 5, 6}  (12 total cells)
  Effort: 7
  Layouts: Rgb8
  cjxl: libjxl HEAD at /home/lilith/work/jxl-efforts/libjxl/build/tools/cjxl
        invoked with `cjxl -d <d> -e 7 <src> <out>`

Configurations:
  ours_w29:    LossyConfig::new(d).with_effort(7)
               → high_d_photo_hint auto-fires (W44-29 default-on)
  ours_nohint: LossyConfig::new(d).with_effort(7)
                 .with_high_d_photo_hint(Some(false))
               → forces EntropyMulTable::reference() (libjxl values)

Method:
  In-process encode via cargo example `w44_77_dump`.
  cjxl reference shelled out per cell, /tmp scratch.
  Per-block dump infrastructure (W44-76 module) gated by
  JXL_W44_76_PER_BLOCK_DUMP=<dir>.  Per-position cost dump gated by
  JXL_DUMP_POS=bx,by.

Findings (TL;DR):
  1. find_best_32x32_transform is structurally at parity with
     libjxl's FindBestFirstLevelDivisionForSquare (line-by-line audit
     in w44_77_find_best_32x32_parity_audit_2026-05-19.md).
  2. W44-76's 96-cell DCT32X16/DCT32X32 mismatch is the intended
     side-effect of W44-29's `high_d_photo_smooth_suppressed`
     entropy_mul table swap.
  3. Disabling W44-29 closes 80 of 96 mismatched cells (per-block
     evidence in w44_77_per_block_after_w29_off_2026-05-19.txt) but
     regresses bytes by +0 to +2423 B per cell — load-bearing.
  4. The strategy alignment and the byte target are *opposed* —
     no single-knob fix exists.

Conclusion: HONEST-STOP per CLAUDE.md rule "Regression on any photo
cell: revert + investigate".  No fix shipped.

