  w44_77_fd_residual_ab_2026-05-19.tsv    bytes A/B with cjxl reference
  w44_77_per_block_after_w29_off_2026-05-19.txt  per-cell diff
  w44_77_find_best_32x32_parity_audit_2026-05-19.md  side-by-side audit
  w44_77_meta_2026-05-19.meta             this file

Follow-on W44-78 plan:
  Hypothesis: a 2-axis tuning search holding W44-29's dct32x32=1.34
  while *lifting* dct16x32/dct32x16 above the libjxl 1.49 ratio (e.g.
  to 1.50-1.60) would re-tip close-races toward DCT32X32 selection
  while keeping W44-29's F-D residual byte savings.  Cells: 1420710 /
  1531677 / 1189261 at d ∈ {4, 5, 6}; grid: dct16x32 ∈
  {1.349, 1.40, 1.45, 1.50, 1.55, 1.60}.  Acceptance: any cell
  achieves -100 B vs current default while no cell regresses > +100 B.
